From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:15:00 -0400
Subject: ui: the 2026 desktop refresh stays on with the testing config off

Every Stedding build so far ran Chromium's field-trial testing config
(testing/variations/fieldtrial_testing_config.json): official builds do
too unless disable_fieldtrial_testing_config is set, and none of ours set
it (privacy Q10, tooling/args). Its "GlowUp" study switched on the seven
features of Chromium's 2026 desktop refresh -- MenuSimplification,
RoundedIcons, TabGroupColorRefresh, TabStripDeclutter, ToolbarGlowUp,
UpdateTabGroupColors, WebuiRefresh2026 -- and every round of the series
was built and measured against that look. With the config off the source
defaults come back: the address chip drew Chromium's old logo where the
mark had been, the first build without it showed (2026-09-09).

The seven are FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT here, each with the same note,
so the decision is in the source rather than in a Google experiment file.
BACKLOG S-57 is the review of each on its merits.

Why: docs/features/privacy.md Q10.
Removable when: upstream ships the refresh by default, or Stedding decides
against a feature in S-57.
